5. Even 'Ramnath Iyer's' 'Law Lexicon' defines a witness as one who gives or is to give evidence in a case. It does not exclude party to suit or proceedings. Be that as it is, it is now well settled that when provision of statute law is plain and clear any narrow construction by process of interpretation annotated by supportive precedents, is not required. Such exercise would be causing damage to the very provision itself. (See
Bhavnagar University v. Palitana Sugar Mitt Pvt. Ltd
). No other ground is urged.
